  Status: draft. \ Local mathematical argument is source-guided; all uses of
  the stress packet decay and the finite selected-scale bridge are explicitly
  conditional on the stated inputs. \ No Lean source was changed.

  <section|Source pin and owned output><label|source-pin-and-owned-output>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Upstream Lean source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Owned files: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/physical-ward-propagation.tex>
    and this evidence file.

    <item>Scope endpoint: global separated-configuration Ward identity
    (<verbatim|Still>), its stress-derived line identities, and the all-grade
    Lie brackets (<verbatim|Brackets>) after transfer of the internal erasure
    property. \ The later A09--A17 / integrated Lorentz-action argument is
    outside this unit.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  item>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence and
  scope>>>|<row|<cell|Angular expression, commutation and collinear
  identity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.angular>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.commutes>,
  <verbatim|YM.Ward.Collinear>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.Still>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Sum.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Walk.lean>>|<cell|Equations
  (1) and (2) use the same positional-derivative plus spin-substitution
  convention. <verbatim|Still> is imposed only on <verbatim|conf>; no
  collision extension is assumed.>>|<row|<cell|Ordered configurations
  dense>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.fills>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Axis.lean>>|<cell|Perturb
  each point by a distinct scalar multiple of one fixed basis vector; each
  pair excludes at most one perturbation parameter.>>|<row|<cell|Connect
  ordered configuration to a line by collision-free coordinate
  walks>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.line>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.pushes>,
  <verbatim|YM.Ward.park1>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.Walk>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Axis.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Walk.lean>>|<cell|Select
  a minimum point in the remaining finite set, make it successively extreme
  in two projections, then zero its non-line coordinates while preserving
  line order. Each segment is an extreme-point bridge and remains in
  <verbatim|conf>.>>|<row|<cell|Analyticity and identity transfer along each
  bridge>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.first_adv>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.last_adv>,
  <verbatim|YM.Ward.channel>, <verbatim|YM.Ward.stood>,
  <verbatim|YM.Ward.along>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Extreme.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Walk.lean>; prose
  <verbatim|sec:physical-ward-analytic-continuation>>|<cell|The global
  theorem now takes the segment-analyticity result as an explicit
  hypothesis/cross-reference. The separate unit proves it from the full
  hierarchy, positive-time representation, endpoint jets and the OS/heat
  translation formula. Smoothness on <verbatim|conf> is not treated as
  sufficient.>>|<row|<cell|Global propagation
  theorem>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Ward.global>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/Axis.lean:130>>|<cell|Exact conclusion: if
  <verbatim|x\<in\>conf n>, then <verbatim|Still W T x> for every finite
  <verbatim|n>, under <verbatim|W.Derivatives>, <verbatim|Collinear>, and
  <verbatim|commutes>. The proof is ordered density, finite walk, then
  continuity on <verbatim|conf>.>>|<row|<cell|A01 local response
  symmetries>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A01.translation_color>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A01.angular_hyper>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A01.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A01.lean>>|<cell|Derives
  color/inclusion/reality/unit/mirror properties from compact-window flux
  identities, translation/reflection/conjugation covariance, and
  conservation. The unit identity explicitly applies conservation after
  deleting the unit insertion.>>|<row|<cell|A02 derivative-shell
  compatibility>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A02.deriv_integral>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A02.answer>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A02.lean>>|<cell|Differentiates
  under a fixed compact shell integral. Uniform domination comes from compact
  support of the cutoff derivative and smoothness on <verbatim|conf>; the two
  derivative terms are the coefficient derivative and the raised insertion
  slot.>>|<row|<cell|A03 all positional jets of line
  response>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A03.all_line>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A03.row_D>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A03.full_jet>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A03.line_native>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A03.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A03.lean>>|<cell|Mixed-cap rows are first proved
  equal to the once-raised row on all of <verbatim|conf> by differentiating
  the moments there. Only the order-zero raised row is evaluated on the line,
  after padding caps and applying <verbatim|LineSum>; induction evaluates
  each further raised row on the line. No line-only identity is transversely
  differentiated.>>|<row|<cell|A04 finite test-row
  recovery>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A04.finite_faithful>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A04.tendsto_of_fitted>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A04.jetsAt>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A04.answer>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A04.lean>>|<cell|Finite-dimensional
  faithful free evaluations reduce to finitely many tests. Fixed-window jet
  convergence gives convergence of each approximating row. A left inverse of
  the limiting injective map makes the fitted moving vector
  converge.>>|<row|<cell|A05 stress and spin readout
  limits>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A05.Observer.gets_translation>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A05.Observer.gets_rotation>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A05.answer>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A05.lean>>|<cell|A
  finite union of observers is chosen before one Track threshold. Compact
  cutoff identities identify their limits with stress-gradient and spin
  readouts; fixed-window jets and stress-meter convergence give the two
  claimed limits.>>|<row|<cell|A06 finite collinear test
  transport>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A06.test_aisle>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A06.test_limit>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A06.moves_limit>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A06.transverse_zero>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A06.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A06.lean>>|<cell|Exact identity: <verbatim|test_k(s,
  aisle_k(q)) = r_k^{m_s} lens_{scaled(k,s)}(q)>. A common finite maximum
  gives convergence on each fixed free vector, then operator convergence for
  the finite-dimensional row maps. The moved tests annihilate both the actual
  derivative and response exactly at each scale. No injectivity of the free
  test family is asserted or used in A06.>>|<row|<cell|A07 transfer of
  erasure>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A07.finite_rows>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A07.eventually_injective>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A07.transfer>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A07.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A07.lean>>|<cell|The free internal covariance
  subspace is finite-dimensional. Free erasure yields finitely many
  separating rows; their actual rows converge on a fixed basis, hence remain
  injective. Pullback by the aligned grade isomorphism transfers zero row-sum
  to zero defect.>>|<row|<cell|A08 differentiated Ward
  brackets>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.A08.orbital_ward>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.orbit_twice>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.double_spin_sub>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.defect_winds>, <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.defect_ward>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A08.answer>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A08.lean>>|<cell|Sign
  check: <verbatim|[X_u,X_v]=-X_[u,v]>, while <verbatim|X_u S=-S(Y_u)>, so
  the orbital commutator contributes <verbatim|+S(Y_[u,v])>. The two spin
  substitutions contribute <verbatim|+S([Y_u,Y_v])>; subtracting gives the
  stated defect. Distinct-slot terms cancel in pairs. The defect is an
  internal <verbatim|Winds> map with zero Ward rows, so erasure kills it at
  large grade; inclusion injectivity descends the identity to every
  grade.>>|<row|<cell|Free collinear classifier
  input>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.Hidden.exposed>,
  <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.Magnitude.charges_quiet>,
  <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.Scenes.scanner>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/{Hidden,Magnitude,Scenes}.lean>>|<cell|The
  detector grade kills every shell-weighted ghost; the quiet-charge
  calculation reduces the scalar derivative response to collinear charges;
  <verbatim|scanner> supplies finite collinear rows. This is a separate
  free-theory producer, not supplied by finite-dimensional detection
  alone.>>|<row|<cell|Free internal-map erasure
  input>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.AwayTeam.erasing>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/AwayTeam.lean>>|<cell|For an alternating
  two-skew-parameter internal map with zero separated Ward rows, this
  supplies the finite grade frame used by A07. Its prerequisites include
  low-motion, stress annihilation and the commuting Ends/statistics
  data.>>|<row|<cell|Outer stress supplier>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Outer.blows>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.pick_price>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.off_label>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.collimated>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.exterior_size>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.track_sale>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.ice>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.line_cost>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.point_cost>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.mass>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.normal>,
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.balanced_mul>, <verbatim|YM.Outer.track_pose>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/ROTATIONS/{Yard,Vanishing,Cove,Thaw,Tunnel,Mass,Patch}.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|exterior_size>
  combines cove pieces with exponents at most <verbatim|-119.5>,
  <verbatim|-972>, <verbatim|-146> or <verbatim|-221.5>, and a damped
  exterior estimate, to obtain <verbatim|Budget(-101)> for the unamplified
  readout. <verbatim|track_pose> contributes exactly <verbatim|exp(100n)>, so
  <verbatim|pick_price> gives <verbatim|Budget(-1)>. <verbatim|blows>
  identifies this readout with the actual insertion packet away from a finite
  null set. The manuscript displays the exponent arithmetic, uses the
  normalized transverse dilation, and distinguishes the panel Fourier gap
  from the compact spatial petal. The positive line/point/exterior estimates
  are supplied by <verbatim|sec:physical-ward-packet-prices>; the fixed-band
  cone estimate is supplied by <verbatim|sec:physical-ward-stress-cone>.>>|<row|<cell|Actual
  consumer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Climb.descends>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Climb/Beams.lean:86--100>>|<cell|Calls
  <verbatim|YM.Ward.global> on the scaled row
  <verbatim|c\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\> \<bullet\> Y> using the
  <verbatim|Crystal.ready> commutation and collinearity fields, then proceeds
  to the separate Spin tilt construction.>>>>>

  <section|Exact analytic boundary><label|exact-analytic-boundary>

  The manuscript proves the finite-configuration propagation, the collinear
  stress-packet estimate, and the finite-level A01--A08 bridges from the
  stated mathematical inputs. The packet calculation uses the already
  reviewed positive line/point/exterior estimates in
  <verbatim|sec:physical-ward-packet-prices> and the fixed-band cone estimate
  in <verbatim|sec:physical-ward-stress-cone>; it derives the remaining
  packet rate by the weighted Cauchy decomposition displayed in the TeX. In
  particular, the four cove exponents are at most <verbatim|-119.5>,
  <verbatim|-972>, <verbatim|-146>, and <verbatim|-221.5>, and the complement
  costs <verbatim|-101>. The exact profile factor <verbatim|exp(100 n)>
  leaves an integrable shell bound <verbatim|C exp(-n)>. The exterior term
  uses positive-time damped spectral control, not an undamped zeroth moment.
  The cove lies where each normalized transverse coordinate is in
  <verbatim|[-1,1]>; the transverse cutoff is one there and supported in
  <verbatim|[-2,2]>. Its normalized dilations are included in both price
  weights.

  The same-slice identity is applied only after the weighted Cauchy and
  damped exterior bounds establish spectral integrability, and the strict
  temporal-gap plus Schwartz bounds establish position-side integrability and
  Fubini. The finite-volume stress response then tends to zero, giving the
  collinear angular identity. This argument uses the actual finite signed
  cluster expansion and coordinate-reflection cancellation, rather than
  identifying an individual cluster with the stress insertion.

  The remaining free-theory inputs are distinct and explicit: the collinear
  classifier <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.Scenes.scanner> and the internal-map
  erasure <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free.AwayTeam.erasing>, with its low-motion,
  stress-annihilation, and commuting Ends/statistics hypotheses. The source
  chain producing them is recorded in the following unit,
  <verbatim|physical-ward-free-classification>. The finite-dimensional
  detector <verbatim|FD.scanner_inj> only detects field polynomials; it does
  not prove either free input. The actual-stress-normalization unit supplies
  the common selected curve, all finite Track/ActLaw tail requests,
  finite-window jet convergence, stress-meter convergence, and the spin-side
  normalization. The manuscript adds the finite algebraic rank step: augment
  the finite selected collinear row map by one functional nonzero on the free
  derivative, pass injectivity from the free map by basiswise convergence,
  and compare the positional response with the derivative. Grade inclusion
  makes the resulting nonzero scalar independent of grade. No downstream
  rotation-action argument is used to obtain that scalar.

  The source theorem <verbatim|YM.Outer.miles> specializes
  <verbatim|YM.Outer.outer> to <verbatim|V>, the seed kernel, stress
  <verbatim|I.J>, positional response <verbatim|I.p>, and spin response
  <verbatim|I.Y>. The orientation premise is <verbatim|H.aligned> and the
  stress-law package is <verbatim|H.planet>. The manuscript supplies the
  packet composition and rate arithmetic, and cites the separately proved
  price units for the estimates used in that composition. No rank or
  continuous-rotation bootstrap is used.

  <section|Literature and checks><label|literature-and-checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read <verbatim|blueprint/background/README.md>; it contains no
    accepted external result for this finite-configuration Ward propagation
    or compact flux packet argument. \ No external literature theorem is
    invoked here.

    <item>Inspected targeted source only:
    <verbatim|Ward/{Axis,Walk,Extreme,Sum}.lean>, <verbatim|Work/A01.lean>
    through <verbatim|Work/A08.lean>, <verbatim|Next/ROTATIONS/{Route,River,
    Stones,Yard,Vanishing,Cove,Tunnel,Mass,Thaw,Frost,Patch,Budget}.lean>,
    <verbatim|Bid/{Angular,Town}.lean>, <verbatim|Climb/Beams.lean>, and
    targeted free declarations in <verbatim|Next/MAXWELL/{Hidden,Magnitude,Scenes,AwayTeam}.lean>.

    <item>No Lean source edits and no Lean build were run.

    <item><verbatim|git diff --no-index --check /dev/null
    \<less\>file\<gtr\>> was run for both owned files; each returned the
    expected difference status for an untracked file and emitted no
    whitespace diagnostics.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run. It stops
    because the shared <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is
    absent in this draft clone; this task does not own that shared metadata
    file.

    <item>No LaTeX build was run; this is a standalone draft fragment pending
    parent integration and its shared macros/environments.
  </itemize-minus>

